  "method": "This batch contains 32 fresh campaign cases: 27 strict nominal improvements and five improved native certificates for AP12 self-host constructions already known at nominal scale 4. The five certificate reductions are identified separately in the manifest; they are not claimed as new nominal bounds.\n\nThe constructions use exact balanced like/unlike antiprism row contacts and marked finite returns, whole-height layer words and vacancy returns, whole-block translations, whole-prism axial subdivisions, and the declared Catalan source-cell returns. Complete source geometry, inherited author credits, marks, frames, all host walls, pair separators and common restoration paths are retained. Classical mechanisms and published source authors retain their attribution; finite construction credit is PingYou Ltd.\n\nThe eight-owner AP4 self-host construction has exact feasible scale 42 - 28 sqrt(2). Its complete endpoint and a six-wall/five-pair contact circuit were independently verified. That circuit proves optimality for the declared fixed contact map only; no global optimum is claimed.\n\nAll 32 packaged records pass both verify_general.py and certify_general.py (64 checks), independent full geometry/source reviews, current public and retained-construction comparisons, and archive checksum/privacy/dependency checks. The trusted batch parser selects exactly 32 native candidates. Final comparison: repository dc0d6f3bea4c1a5d3ca1845dd1793fd5d9a19828 and site build 2026-10-15 11:27. Thirty cases were previously unheld by PingYou in the selected site records; two improve already-held cases. Submission does not itself establish acceptance.\n\nArchive SHA256: c1c7eb625dee4579f3dcacafda01ecf221e6d0d1c3b88821c3ad5ca73f83aafc\nArchive size: 15,670,552 bytes.\n\nPublication under the repository's MIT license is authorized.",
